// ForkAgentWithBody Fork a public agent into a namespace the caller may create in.
//
// Makes a private copy of a public agent: a new agent in `namespace`, under the origin's name unless `name` gives another, that records the origin and the published version it was taken from, for good. A fork is never public (`PATCH` to public answers `409 fork-stays-private`). The fork is answered `202` with `forkState: copying`: a worker then copies from the origin's repository the forked release's commit and its history, when the release was tagged and scanned, and nothing else (no other branch or tag; objects copied rather than shared), writes one commit, "Fork of ns/name@version", on top of it or, with nothing copied, from the release's archive, that renames the manifest into the fork's namespace, tags it with the origin's version and submits it through the pipeline like any submission, charged like one. `forkState` is then `ready`, or `failed` with `forkDetail` saying why. The origin must be readable, public, neither quarantined nor blocked, and have a published version; the caller must be able to create a private agent in `namespace` (its owner, or an active member of the organization), within its agent quota and private-agent cap. A name the namespace already has answers `409 name-taken`; one a deleted agent holds, `409 name-held`.
